      <div class="rm-sec">
        <h5>The dataset</h5>
        <p>196 countries × 31 birth cohorts (1970–2000) × both sexes = <b>12,152 observations</b>,
        6,076 per sex, with 11 environment features. Height is NCD-RisC (Lancet 2020), mean height
        at age 19, so a birth cohort is the measurement year minus 19. Development indicators come
        from the World Bank, and food supply from FAO via Our World in Data. Every feature is
        averaged across the childhood window — birth year to birth year + 10.</p>
