      <div class="rm-sec">
        <h5>Limitations</h5>
        <p>All associations are <b>ecological</b>. These are country-level relationships and they do
        not establish individual causation. Features with heavy missingness — sanitation 29.1%,
        breastfeeding 26.5%, Gini 14.3% — are median-imputed, so the signal survives but the noise
        is real. North Korea has no sanitation, healthcare-spend or GDP series at all.</p>
        <p><b>The Korea mirror uses a different source from the rest of the deck</b>, and deliberately.
        NCD-RisC cannot resolve the comparison: its North Korea estimate carries the widest uncertainty
        interval of all 200 countries — 173.7 cm for the 1996 cohort with a 95% CI of <b>162.0 to 186.3</b>,
