        atlas and door frame keep the NCD-RisC figure, so North Korea reads differently there.</p>
        <p>Height is not presented here as a goal. Taller is not better. The claim is narrower: the
        average height of a country's children is an unusually honest summary of how well that
        country fed, healed and protected them.</p>
