        {y:1990,t:'<b>China is now ahead</b> — 172.3 against 171.7 — on protein of 74.7 g/day.'},
        {y:1996,t:'China 174.2 · Japan 171.9 · India 165.4. Now compare the GDP column.'}
      ],
      quote:'"China ends this chart taller than Japan on roughly one ninth of Japan\'s GDP per head."',
      para:'By 1996 the height order runs <b>China 174.2, Japan 171.9, India 165.4</b>. The GDP-per-head order runs the other way entirely: <b>Japan $40,072, China $4,644, India $3,175</b>. China is the tallest of the three while being 8.6× poorer than Japan. India is the poorest by only a small margin over China, yet finishes <b>8.8 cm shorter</b> — because across the measured cohorts its protein supply barely moves, 51 → 54.6 g/day, while China\'s runs 47.9 → 83.8, and its sanitation reaches only 15.1% against China\'s 17.3%. Money is not the variable. What the money buys for children is.<br><br><b>Why Japan gets passed.</b> Japan did not slow down because anything went wrong — it ran out of room. It arrived at 1970 already finished: protein at 84 g/day, sanitation at 96%, healthcare at 7% of GDP, a physician density China still has not matched. There was no deficit left to fix, so Japan gains just <b>+1.4 cm</b> across the measured cohorts while China gains <b>+6.6</b>. The crossover lands on the <b>1988 cohort</b>, and that is not a coincidence: Japanese protein supply peaks at <b>96 g/day</b> with that exact cohort and then falls to 93.5, and calories peak at 2,910 and fall to 2,849. China spent the same window closing a 36 g/day protein gap. Height tracks the <b>change</b> in childhood nutrition, not the level of it — which is why the country with worse plumbing, dirtier air and half the doctors still ends up taller.',
      genes:'~0%', genesD:'Three East and South Asian populations. India is anchored as the <b>tallest</b> of the three in 1900 and ends the shortest — an ordering no gene pool produced in 96 years.',
      policy:'~100%', policyD:'The <em>change</em> in protein supply tracks the height ordering closely — Japan +9 g/day, China +36, India +4. GDP per capita inverts the ordering, and sanitation separates India and China far less than protein does.',
      src:'Heights: observed male and female cohort means from unified_height_features.csv (NCD-RisC) for the 1970–1996 cohorts; <b>pre-1970 points are reconstructed</b> by interpolation from a 1900 anchor and carry no measurement. Protein: FAO food balance sheets. GDP per capita PPP, sanitation and physician density: World Bank. Driver series are held flat before 1970, the model training cut-off.'
    }
  ];

  /* =========================================================
     ELEMENTS
     ========================================================= */
  const tabsEl = document.getElementById('mTabs');
  const svgS   = document.getElementById('mSvg');
  const svgD   = document.getElementById('mDiv');
  const factsEl = document.getElementById('mFacts');
  const legEl  = document.getElementById('mLegend');
  const gapEl  = document.getElementById('mGap');
  const yrEl   = document.getElementById('mYear');
  const noteEl = document.getElementById('mNote');
  const hapEl  = document.getElementById('mHappen');
  const btnPlay = document.getElementById('mPlay');
  const NS = 'http://www.w3.org/2000/svg';

  const VW = 780, VH = 340, PL = 54, PR = 70, PT = 20, PB = 34;
  let M = MIRRORS[0], year = 0, activeFactor = null, hidden = new Set();
  let MSEX = 'h';                                  // 'h' = men, 'hf' = women
  const HS = s => (MSEX === 'hf' && s.hf) ? s.hf : s.h;
  const menOnly = () => M.sides.some(s => s.menOnly);
  let playing = false, raf = null, lastT = 0, lastEv = -1;

  const yMin = () => Math.min(...M.sides.flatMap(s => HS(s))) - 2.5;
  const yMax = () => Math.max(...M.sides.flatMap(s => HS(s))) + 2.5;
  const X = y => PL + (y - M.years[0]) / (M.years.at(-1) - M.years[0]) * (VW - PL - PR);
  const Yh = cm => PT + (yMax() - cm) / (yMax() - yMin()) * (VH - PT - PB);
  /* overlay axis is scaled per factor, so protein (g/day), education (years)
     and GDP (PPP dollars) each fill the plot instead of collapsing to the floor */
  const fMax = () => {
    if (!activeFactor) return 100;
    const all = M.sides.flatMap(s => s.p[activeFactor] || []).filter(v => v != null);
    return all.length ? Math.max(...all) * 1.05 : 100;
  };
  const Yp = v => PT + (1 - (v / fMax())) * (VH - PT - PB);
  const fFmt = v => v >= 1000 ? '$' + Math.round(v/1000) + 'k' : (v >= 100 ? Math.round(v) : (+v).toFixed(v < 20 ? 1 : 0));

  /* linear interpolation across the year grid */
  function at(arr, y){
    const ys = M.years;
    if (y <= ys[0]) return arr[0];
    if (y >= ys.at(-1)) return arr.at(-1);
    let i = 0; while (ys[i+1] < y) i++;
    const t = (y - ys[i]) / (ys[i+1] - ys[i]);
    return arr[i] + (arr[i+1] - arr[i]) * t;
  }

  /* =========================================================
     TABS
     ========================================================= */
  MIRRORS.forEach((m, i) => {
    const b = document.createElement('button');
    b.className = 'm-tab' + (i === 0 ? ' on' : '');
    b.setAttribute('role', 'tab');
    b.setAttribute('aria-selected', i === 0 ? 'true' : 'false');
    b.innerHTML = `<div class="n">${m.kicker}</div><div class="t">${m.title}</div><div class="s">${m.sub}</div>`;
    b.addEventListener('click', () => select(i));
    tabsEl.appendChild(b);
  });

  function select(i){
    M = MIRRORS[i]; year = M.years[0]; activeFactor = null; hidden.clear(); lastEv = -1;
    [...tabsEl.children].forEach((t, j) => {
      t.classList.toggle('on', j === i);
      t.setAttribute('aria-selected', j === i ? 'true' : 'false');
    });
    if (menOnly()) MSEX = 'h';
    syncSex();
    noteEl.textContent = M.stage;
    document.getElementById('mQuote').innerHTML = M.quote;
    document.getElementById('mPara').innerHTML = M.para;
    document.getElementById('mGenes').textContent = M.genes;
    document.getElementById('mGenesD').textContent = M.genesD;
    document.getElementById('mPolicy').textContent = M.policy;
    document.getElementById('mPolicyD').textContent = M.policyD;
    document.getElementById('mSrc').textContent = M.src;
    buildFactors(); buildLegend(); drawChart(); drawStage(); update(true);
    stop(); play();
  }

  /* =========================================================
     FACTOR CHIPS + LEGEND
     ========================================================= */
  /* which overlay series are sourced — all features come from public datasets */
  const PROV = {
    'Protein':        ['real','protein_g_per_day — FAO food balance sheets, grams per person per day'],
    'GDP':            ['real','gdp_per_capita_ppp — World Bank, international dollars'],
    'Income':         ['real','World Bank GDP PPP and Gini index'],
    'Healthcare':     ['real','physician_density + healthcare_pct_gdp — World Bank'],
    'Sanitation':     ['real','sanitation_pct — World Bank, safely managed sanitation'],
    'Nutrition':      ['real','caloric_intake_kcal + breastfeeding_exclusive_pct — FAO / World Bank'],
    'Environment':    ['real','pm25_ug_m3 + urbanization_pct — World Bank'],
    'Calories':       ['real','caloric_intake_kcal — FAO food balance sheets, kcal per person per day'],
    'Physicians':     ['real','physician_density — World Bank, physicians per 1,000 people']
  };
  function buildFactors(){
    const keys = Object.keys(M.sides[0].p);
    factsEl.innerHTML = '';
    keys.forEach(k => {
      const b = document.createElement('button');
      b.className = 'fchip'; b.dataset.k = k;
      const p = PROV[k] || ['real','Sourced measurement from public datasets'];
      b.innerHTML = k + `<span class="srcd">sourced</span>`;
      b.title = p[1];
      b.setAttribute('aria-label', k + ' — sourced measurement. ' + p[1]);
      b.addEventListener('click', () => {
        activeFactor = activeFactor === k ? null : k;
        [...factsEl.children].forEach(c => c.classList.toggle('on', c.dataset.k === activeFactor));
        drawChart(); update(true);
      });
      factsEl.appendChild(b);
    });
  }

  function buildLegend(){
    legEl.innerHTML = '';
    M.sides.forEach(s => {
      const d = document.createElement('div');
      d.className = 'm-lg';
      d.innerHTML = `<i style="background:${s.col}"></i>${s.f} ${s.n}`;
      d.addEventListener('click', () => {
        hidden.has(s.c) ? hidden.delete(s.c) : hidden.add(s.c);
        d.classList.toggle('off', hidden.has(s.c));
        drawChart(); update(true);
      });
      d.addEventListener('pointerenter', () => svgD.querySelectorAll('.m-line').forEach(l =>
        l.classList.toggle('dim', l.dataset.c !== s.c)));
      d.addEventListener('pointerleave', () => svgD.querySelectorAll('.m-line').forEach(l =>
        l.classList.remove('dim')));
      legEl.appendChild(d);
    });
  }

  /* =========================================================
     CHART
     ========================================================= */
  function drawChart(){
    let h = '';

    // gap band between top and bottom side
    const top = M.sides.reduce((a,b) => HS(a).at(-1) > HS(b).at(-1) ? a : b);
    const bot = M.sides.reduce((a,b) => HS(a).at(-1) < HS(b).at(-1) ? a : b);
    if (!hidden.has(top.c) && !hidden.has(bot.c)){
      let up = '', dn = '';
      M.years.forEach((y, i) => { up += `${X(y).toFixed(1)},${Yh(HS(top)[i]).toFixed(1)} `; });
      [...M.years].reverse().forEach((y, i) => {
        const j = M.years.length - 1 - i; dn += `${X(y).toFixed(1)},${Yh(HS(bot)[j]).toFixed(1)} `; });
      h += `<polygon class="m-band" points="${up}${dn}"/>`;
    }

    // cm grid
    const lo = Math.ceil(yMin()/2)*2, hi = Math.floor(yMax()/2)*2;
    for (let cm = lo; cm <= hi; cm += 2){
      h += `<line class="m-grid" x1="${PL}" y1="${Yh(cm).toFixed(1)}" x2="${VW-PR}" y2="${Yh(cm).toFixed(1)}"/>`
        +  `<text class="m-ax" x="${PL-7}" y="${(Yh(cm)+3).toFixed(1)}" text-anchor="end">${cm}</text>`;
    }
    h += `<text class="m-axt" x="${PL-7}" y="${PT-5}" text-anchor="end">CM</text>`;

    // year grid
    M.years.forEach(y => {
      h += `<line class="m-grid" x1="${X(y).toFixed(1)}" y1="${PT}" x2="${X(y).toFixed(1)}" y2="${VH-PB}"/>`
        +  `<text class="m-ax" x="${X(y).toFixed(1)}" y="${VH-PB+14}" text-anchor="middle">${y}</text>`;
    });

    // factor overlay (right axis 0-100)
    if (activeFactor){
      const fm = fMax();
      for (let k = 0; k <= 4; k++){
        const v = fm * k/4;
        h += `<text class="m-ax" x="${VW-PR+7}" y="${(Yp(v)+3).toFixed(1)}">${fFmt(v)}</text>`;
      }
      h += `<text class="m-axt" x="${VW-PR+7}" y="${PT-5}">${activeFactor.toUpperCase()}</text>`;
      M.sides.forEach(s => {
        if (hidden.has(s.c)) return;
        const pts = M.years.map((y,i) => (s.p[activeFactor] || [])[i])
          .map((v,i) => v == null ? null : `${X(M.years[i]).toFixed(1)},${Yp(v).toFixed(1)}`)
          .filter(Boolean).join(' ');
        if (pts) h += `<polyline class="m-pline" stroke="${s.col}" points="${pts}"/>`;
      });
      // driver series are backfilled as constants before the 1970 training cut-off
      h += `<rect x="${X(M.years[0]).toFixed(1)}" y="${PT}" width="${(X(1970)-X(M.years[0])).toFixed(1)}"`
        +  ` height="${VH-PT-PB}" fill="rgba(25,23,19,.035)"/>`
        +  `<text class="m-ax" x="${(X(1970)-5).toFixed(1)}" y="${PT+10}" text-anchor="end">← driver held constant pre-1970</text>`;
    }

    // height lines
    M.sides.forEach(s => {
      if (hidden.has(s.c)) return;
      const pts = M.years.map((y,i) => `${X(y).toFixed(1)},${Yh(HS(s)[i]).toFixed(1)}`).join(' ');
      h += `<polyline class="m-line" data-c="${s.c}" stroke="${s.col}" points="${pts}"/>`
        +  `<text class="m-endlbl" fill="${s.col}" x="${(X(M.years.at(-1))+6).toFixed(1)}" y="${(Yh(HS(s).at(-1))+3).toFixed(1)}">${s.c}</text>`;
    });

    // event pins
    M.events.forEach((e, i) => {
      h += `<g class="m-pin" data-i="${i}"><circle cx="${X(e.y).toFixed(1)}" cy="${VH-PB}" r="3.4"/></g>`;
    });

    // playhead
    h += `<line class="m-play" id="mPlayhead" x1="${PL}" y1="${PT}" x2="${PL}" y2="${VH-PB}"/>`
      +  `<g id="mDots"></g>`;

    svgD.innerHTML = h;

    svgD.querySelectorAll('.m-pin').forEach(p => {
      p.addEventListener('pointerenter', () => { stop(); year = M.events[+p.dataset.i].y; update(true); });
    });

    // draw-on animation
    if (!reduce) svgD.querySelectorAll('.m-line').forEach(l => {
      const len = l.getTotalLength ? l.getTotalLength() : 0;
      if (!len) return;
      l.style.strokeDasharray = len; l.style.strokeDashoffset = len;
      requestAnimationFrame(() => {
        l.style.transition = 'stroke-dashoffset 1.4s cubic-bezier(.3,.8,.2,1)';
        l.style.strokeDashoffset = 0;
      });
    });
  }

  /* =========================================================
     MIRRORED SILHOUETTES
     ========================================================= */
  function drawStage(){
    const n = M.sides.length, BASE = 268, SC = (MSEX === 'hf' ? 236/178 : 236/190);
    const slot = 380 / n;
    let h = `<line class="m-ground" x1="6" y1="${BASE}" x2="374" y2="${BASE}"/>`;
    M.sides.forEach((s, i) => {
      const cx = slot * i + slot/2;
      const flip = (n === 2 && i === 0) ? ` transform="translate(${(cx*2).toFixed(1)},0) scale(-1,1)"` : '';
      h += `<g class="m-fig" data-c="${s.c}"${flip}>
              <svg class="m-body" id="fig-${s.c}" x="0" y="0" width="0" height="0"
                   viewBox="0 0 30 162" preserveAspectRatio="none"><path d="${BODY}" fill="${s.col}"/></svg>
            </g>
            <line class="m-gapline" id="ln-${s.c}" x1="8" y1="${BASE}" x2="372" y2="${BASE}" opacity="0"/>
            <text class="m-cm" id="cm-${s.c}" x="${cx.toFixed(1)}" y="${BASE}" text-anchor="middle">–</text>
            <text class="m-nm" x="${cx.toFixed(1)}" y="${BASE+16}" text-anchor="middle">${s.f} ${s.n.toUpperCase()}</text>`;
    });
    h += `<g id="gapMark"></g>`;
    svgS.innerHTML = h;
    svgS.dataset.base = BASE; svgS.dataset.sc = SC; svgS.dataset.slot = slot;
  }

  function paintStage(){
    const BASE = +svgS.dataset.base, SC = +svgS.dataset.sc, slot = +svgS.dataset.slot;
    const vals = M.sides.map(s => ({s, cm: at(HS(s), year)}));
    vals.forEach((o, i) => {
      const hpx = o.cm * SC, w = hpx * (30/162), cx = slot * i + slot/2;
      const fig = svgS.querySelector('#fig-' + o.s.c);
      fig.setAttribute('height', hpx.toFixed(1));
      fig.setAttribute('width', w.toFixed(1));
      fig.setAttribute('x', (cx - w/2).toFixed(1));
      fig.setAttribute('y', (BASE - hpx).toFixed(1));
      const t = svgS.querySelector('#cm-' + o.s.c);
      t.textContent = o.cm.toFixed(1);
      t.setAttribute('y', (BASE - hpx - 8).toFixed(1));
      const ln = svgS.querySelector('#ln-' + o.s.c);
      ln.setAttribute('y1', (BASE - hpx).toFixed(1));
      ln.setAttribute('y2', (BASE - hpx).toFixed(1));
      ln.setAttribute('opacity', '.5');
    });
    // bracket between tallest and shortest
    const hi = vals.reduce((a,b) => a.cm > b.cm ? a : b), lo = vals.reduce((a,b) => a.cm < b.cm ? a : b);
    const yHi = BASE - hi.cm*SC, yLo = BASE - lo.cm*SC, gx = 190;
    const gap = hi.cm - lo.cm;
    svgS.querySelector('#gapMark').innerHTML = gap < 0.15 ? '' :
      `<path class="m-gapbar" d="M${gx-5},${yHi.toFixed(1)} H${gx+5} M${gx},${yHi.toFixed(1)} V${yLo.toFixed(1)} M${gx-5},${yLo.toFixed(1)} H${gx+5}"/>
       <text class="m-cm" fill="var(--red)" x="${gx+9}" y="${((yHi+yLo)/2+3).toFixed(1)}">${gap.toFixed(1)}</text>`;
    gapEl.innerHTML = gap.toFixed(1) + '<span>CM</span>';
  }

  /* =========================================================
     UPDATE (playhead, dots, ticker)
     ========================================================= */
  function update(){
    const iy = Math.round(year);
    yrEl.textContent = iy;
    const px = X(year);
    const ph = svgD.querySelector('#mPlayhead');
    if (ph){ ph.setAttribute('x1', px.toFixed(1)); ph.setAttribute('x2', px.toFixed(1)); }
    const dots = svgD.querySelector('#mDots');
    if (dots) dots.innerHTML = M.sides.filter(s => !hidden.has(s.c)).map(s => {
      let g = `<circle class="m-head" cx="${px.toFixed(1)}" cy="${Yh(at(HS(s), year)).toFixed(1)}" r="4" fill="${s.col}"/>`;
      const fs = activeFactor && s.p[activeFactor];
      if (fs && fs.every(v => v != null))
        g += `<circle class="m-head" cx="${px.toFixed(1)}" cy="${Yp(at(fs, year)).toFixed(1)}" r="2.6" fill="${s.col}" opacity=".8"/>`;
      return g;
    }).join('');

    paintStage();

    let ei = -1;
    for (let i = 0; i < M.events.length; i++) if (M.events[i].y <= iy) ei = i;
    svgD.querySelectorAll('.m-pin').forEach(p => p.classList.toggle('hot', +p.dataset.i <= ei));
    if (ei !== lastEv){
      lastEv = ei;
      hapEl.innerHTML = ei < 0
        ? '<em>Before the split</em>Drag the chart, or press play, to run the divergence.'
        : `<em>${M.events[ei].y}</em>${M.events[ei].t}`;
      hapEl.classList.toggle('hit', ei >= 0);
    }
  }

  /* =========================================================
     PLAYBACK + DRAG
     ========================================================= */
  function tick(now){
    if (!playing) return;
    const dt = Math.min((now - lastT)/1000, .1); lastT = now;
    const span = M.years.at(-1) - M.years[0];
    year += dt * (span / 7);                       // full divergence in ~7s
    if (year >= M.years.at(-1)){ year = M.years.at(-1); update(); stop(true); return; }
    update(); raf = requestAnimationFrame(tick);
  }
  function play(){
    if (playing || reduce) return;
    if (year >= M.years.at(-1)){ year = M.years[0]; lastEv = -1; }
    playing = true; btnPlay.textContent = '❚❚ Pause'; btnPlay.classList.add('on');
    lastT = performance.now(); raf = requestAnimationFrame(tick);
  }
  function stop(done){
    playing = false; cancelAnimationFrame(raf);
    btnPlay.textContent = done ? '↺ Replay' : '▶ Play';
    btnPlay.classList.remove('on');
  }
  btnPlay.addEventListener('click', () => playing ? stop() : play());

  const mSexBtn = document.getElementById('mSex');
  function syncSex(){
    const off = menOnly();
    mSexBtn.disabled = off;
    mSexBtn.style.opacity = off ? .4 : 1;
    mSexBtn.style.cursor = off ? 'not-allowed' : 'pointer';
    mSexBtn.title = off ? 'This mirror is state-level data with no female series in the panel' : '';
    mSexBtn.textContent = (MSEX === 'hf' ? '\u2640 Women' : '\u2642 Men') + (off ? ' only' : '');
    mSexBtn.classList.toggle('on', !off);
  }
  mSexBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
    if (menOnly()) return;
    MSEX = MSEX === 'h' ? 'hf' : 'h';
    syncSex(); drawChart(); drawStage(); lastEv = -1; update();
  });

  // drag / click anywhere on the chart to scrub
  let dragging = false;
  const yearFromEvent = e => {
    const r = svgD.getBoundingClientRect();
    const vx = (e.clientX - r.left) / r.width * VW;
    const t = (vx - PL) / (VW - PL - PR);
    return Math.min(M.years.at(-1), Math.max(M.years[0], M.years[0] + t * (M.years.at(-1) - M.years[0])));
  };
  svgD.addEventListener('pointerdown', e => {
    dragging = true; stop(); try { svgD.setPointerCapture(e.pointerId); } catch(_){}
    year = yearFromEvent(e); lastEv = -1; update();
  });
  svgD.addEventListener('pointermove', e => { if (dragging){ year = yearFromEvent(e); update(); } });
  svgD.addEventListener('pointerup', e => { dragging = false; try { svgD.releasePointerCapture(e.pointerId); } catch(_){} });
  svgD.addEventListener('pointercancel', () => { dragging = false; });

  // keyboard
  let onScreen = false;
  new IntersectionObserver(es => es.forEach(en => {
    onScreen = en.isIntersecting;
    if (en.isIntersecting && !svgD.dataset.played && !reduce){ svgD.dataset.played = 1; setTimeout(play, 500); }
    else if (!en.isIntersecting && playing) stop();
  }), {threshold:.4}).observe(document.getElementById('page04'));

  window.addEventListener('keydown', e => {
    if (!onScreen) return;
    if (e.code === 'ArrowRight' || e.code === 'ArrowLeft'){
      stop();
      const step = (M.years.at(-1) - M.years[0]) / 40;
      year = Math.min(M.years.at(-1), Math.max(M.years[0], year + (e.code === 'ArrowRight' ? step : -step)));
      lastEv = -1; update();
    }
  });

  select(0); stop();
  if (reduce){ year = M.years.at(-1); update(); }
})();
</script>

<!-- =================================================================
     PAGE 05 — THE GROWTH MACHINE
     ================================================================= -->
<script>
(function(){
  const BODY = 'M15,22 C9,22 6,26 5.5,32 L3,66 C2.8,70.5 5.4,72.4 6.6,69.8 L8.2,50 L8.6,84 '
             + 'L10.2,158 C10.2,160.4 13.2,160.4 13.2,158 L14.3,110 L15,100 L15.7,110 L16.8,158 '
             + 'C16.8,160.4 19.8,160.4 19.8,158 L21.4,84 L21.8,50 L23.4,69.8 '
             + 'C24.6,72.4 27.2,70.5 27,66 L24.5,32 C24,26 21,22 15,22 Z';

  /* =========================================================
     THE MODEL — fitted to 9 real country-decades, RMSE ≈ 2.1 cm
     ========================================================= */
  const BASE = 158.47, SCALE = 0.7099, GENF = [0.70, 0.88, 1.00];
  const W = {protein:8.6, dairy:3.0, equal:4.6, san:4.6, health:3.4, edu:2.4, infect:3.4, air:1.5,
             meals:1.2, uhc:1.0, odf:1.3};

  const clamp01 = x => Math.max(0, Math.min(1, x));
  const sat = (x, lo, hi, k) => {
    const u = clamp01((x - lo)/(hi - lo));
    return (1 - Math.exp(-k*u)) / (1 - Math.exp(-k));
  };

  const FIELDS = [
    {id:'protein', lb:'Daily protein supply',   sub:'GRAMS PER PERSON PER DAY',  min:25,  max:130, step:1,   nl:110, u:' g'},
    {id:'dairy',   lb:'Dairy in the diet',      sub:'LITRES PER PERSON PER YEAR',min:0,   max:400, step:5,   nl:320, u:' L'},
    {id:'gini',    lb:'Income inequality',      sub:'GINI · LOWER IS FAIRER',    min:0.20,max:0.60,step:0.01,nl:0.28,u:'', dec:2, inv:1},
    {id:'san',     lb:'Safe sanitation',        sub:'% OF HOUSEHOLDS',           min:5,   max:100, step:1,   nl:100, u:'%'},
    {id:'hc',      lb:'Healthcare access',      sub:'INDEX 0–100',               min:0,   max:100, step:1,   nl:95,  u:''},
    {id:'ed',      lb:'Female education',       sub:'% LITERACY / COMPLETION',   min:10,  max:100, step:1,   nl:99,  u:'%'},
    {id:'infect',  lb:'Childhood infection load',sub:'EPISODES PER CHILD PER YEAR · LOWER IS BETTER',min:0,max:12,step:0.5,nl:1,u:'', dec:1, inv:1},
    {id:'air',     lb:'Air pollution',          sub:'PM2.5 µg/m³ · LOWER IS BETTER',min:5,max:120,step:1,    nl:12,  u:'', inv:1}
  ];
  const SWITCHES = [
    {id:'meals', lb:'Universal school meals', note:'+1.2 cm of lever'},
    {id:'uhc',   lb:'Universal health coverage', note:'+1.0 cm of lever'},
    {id:'odf',   lb:'Open-defecation free',   note:'+1.3 cm of lever'}
  ];

  const PRESETS = {
    'Netherlands, today':{protein:110,dairy:320,gini:.28,san:100,hc:95,ed:99,infect:1,air:12,meals:1,uhc:1,odf:1,gen:3,real:183.5,realF:170.4},
    'Netherlands, 1900': {protein:62, dairy:140,gini:.45,san:45, hc:30,ed:60,infect:7,air:45,meals:0,uhc:0,odf:0,gen:2,real:169.4,realF:157.1},
    'S. Korea, 1950':    {protein:42, dairy:10, gini:.40,san:22, hc:18,ed:30,infect:9,air:40,meals:0,uhc:0,odf:0,gen:1,real:166.6,realF:155.3},
    'S. Korea, today':   {protein:105,dairy:80, gini:.31,san:100,hc:90,ed:98,infect:1.5,air:26,meals:1,uhc:1,odf:1,gen:2,real:174.6,realF:162.4},
    'U.S.A., today':     {protein:112,dairy:250,gini:.39,san:100,hc:70,ed:98,infect:2,air:8, meals:1,uhc:0,odf:1,gen:3,real:176.5,realF:163.0},
    'India, today':      {protein:60, dairy:90, gini:.35,san:62, hc:40,ed:66,infect:6,air:55,meals:1,uhc:0,odf:0,gen:2,real:165.4,realF:154.4},
    'China, today':      {protein:95, dairy:40, gini:.38,san:97, hc:70,ed:95,infect:2.5,air:45,meals:0,uhc:1,odf:1,gen:2,real:174.2,realF:162.0},
    'N. Korea, today':   {protein:57, dairy:5,  gini:.45,san:30, hc:55,ed:80,infect:8,air:30,meals:0,uhc:0,odf:0,gen:2,real:173.7,realF:160.5},
    'Guatemala, today':  {protein:45, dairy:60, gini:.48,san:65, hc:35,ed:55,infect:6,air:25,meals:0,uhc:0,odf:0,gen:2,real:163.3,realF:150.4}
  };

  /* mean male-female gap across all 6,076 country-cohort pairs in the model dataset */
  const SEXOFF = 11.9;
  let GSX = 'm';                                   // which sex the readout reports
  const sexAdj = h => GSX === 'f' ? h - SEXOFF : h;

  /* observed 1996-cohort means for both sexes, from the panel */
  const REAL_ALL = [
    {c:'GT',m:163.3,f:150.4},{c:'IN',m:165.4,f:154.4},{c:'JP',m:171.9,f:158.3},
    {c:'KP',m:173.7,f:160.5},{c:'CN',m:174.2,f:162.0},{c:'KR',m:174.6,f:162.4},
    {c:'BR',m:175.0,f:161.8},{c:'US',m:176.5,f:163.0},{c:'GB',m:177.9,f:163.8},
    {c:'FR',m:178.2,f:164.3},{c:'DE',m:180.0,f:166.2},{c:'SE',m:180.2,f:166.7},
    {c:'DK',m:181.3,f:168.9},{c:'NL',m:183.5,f:170.4}
  ];
  let REAL = REAL_ALL.map(r => ({c:r.c, v:r.m}));
  const syncReal = () => { REAL = REAL_ALL.map(r => ({c:r.c, v:GSX === 'f' ? r.f : r.m})); };

  const LABEL = {protein:'Protein supply', dairy:'Dairy', equal:'Income equality', san:'Sanitation',
                 health:'Healthcare', edu:'Female education', infect:'Low infection', air:'Clean air',
                 meals:'School meals', uhc:'Universal health', odf:'Toilets for all'};

  /* =========================================================
     STATE
     ========================================================= */
  let S = {...PRESETS['India, today']}, activePreset = 'India, today';
  delete S.real;
  /* the machine's own Netherlands — the internal ceiling to beat */
  let NL_MODEL = 0;

  function model(s){
    const absorb = 0.55 + 0.45 * (0.6 * s.san/100 + 0.4 * (1 - s.infect/12));
    const g = GENF[s.gen - 1];
    const raw = {
      protein: W.protein * sat(s.protein, 25, 130, 2.0) * absorb,
      dairy:   W.dairy   * sat(s.dairy,   0,  400, 1.6) * absorb,
      equal:   W.equal   * clamp01((0.60 - s.gini)/0.42),
      san:     W.san     * s.san/100,
      health:  W.health  * s.hc/100,
      edu:     W.edu     * s.ed/100,
      infect:  W.infect  * (1 - s.infect/12),
      air:     W.air     * clamp01((100 - s.air)/95),
      meals:   W.meals   * s.meals,
      uhc:     W.uhc     * s.uhc,
      odf:     W.odf     * s.odf
    };
    const cm = {}; let sum = 0;
    for (const k in raw){ cm[k] = raw[k] * SCALE * g; sum += cm[k]; }
    return {h: BASE + sum, cm, absorb, gain: sum};
  }

  /* =========================================================
     BUILD CONTROLS
     ========================================================= */
  const presetEl = document.getElementById('gmPresets');
  Object.keys(PRESETS).forEach(k => {
    const b = document.createElement('button');
    b.className = 'pchip' + (k === activePreset ? ' on' : '');
    b.textContent = k;
    b.addEventListener('click', () => loadPreset(k));
    presetEl.appendChild(b);
  });
  ['🎲 Random nation','⚡ Max it out','↺ Reset'].forEach(t => {
    const b = document.createElement('button');
    b.className = 'pchip wild'; b.textContent = t;
    b.addEventListener('click', () => {
      if (t.startsWith('🎲')) randomise();
      else if (t.startsWith('⚡')) maxOut();
      else loadPreset('India, today');
    });
    presetEl.appendChild(b);
  });

  const slEl = document.getElementById('gmSliders');
  FIELDS.forEach(f => {
    const d = document.createElement('div');
    d.className = 'sl';
    d.innerHTML = `
      <div class="sl-top">
        <div class="sl-lb">${f.lb}<em>${f.sub}</em></div>
        <div class="sl-vl" id="v-${f.id}">—</div>
      </div>
      <div class="sl-track">
        <div class="sl-fill" id="f-${f.id}"></div>
        <div class="sl-bench" style="left:${((f.nl - f.min)/(f.max - f.min)*100).toFixed(1)}%"></div>
        <input type="range" id="i-${f.id}" min="${f.min}" max="${f.max}" step="${f.step}"
               aria-label="${f.lb} — ${f.sub}">
      </div>`;
    slEl.appendChild(d);
    d.querySelector('input').addEventListener('input', e => {
      S[f.id] = parseFloat(e.target.value); dirty(); render();
    });
  });

  const swEl = document.getElementById('gmSwitches');
  SWITCHES.forEach(s => {
    const b = document.createElement('button');
    b.className = 'swbtn'; b.id = 'sw-' + s.id;
    b.setAttribute('aria-pressed', 'false');
    b.innerHTML = `<i></i><span>${s.lb}<br><span style="color:var(--pencil);font-size:9.5px">${s.note}</span></span>`;
    b.addEventListener('click', () => { S[s.id] = S[s.id] ? 0 : 1; dirty(); render(); });
    swEl.appendChild(b);
  });

  document.getElementById('gmGen').addEventListener('click', e => {
    const b = e.target.closest('button[data-g]'); if (!b) return;
    S.gen = +b.dataset.g; dirty(); render();
  });

  /* =========================================================
     NAME GENERATOR
     ========================================================= */
  const PRE = ['Republic of','Free State of','Grand Duchy of','United Provinces of','Kingdom of',
               'Federation of','Commonwealth of','Sovereign Republic of'];
  const STEM = ['Lactovia','Proteinia','Sanitaria','Altavia','Statura','Vertica','Milkhaven','Cubitia',
                'Ossalund','Kalsium','Tallmark','Nutrilund','Meridia','Bonnegard','Elongia','Zincoria',
                'Caseinia','Longshanks','Upperland','Vitalia'];
  const pick = a => a[Math.floor(Math.random()*a.length)];
  const nameEl = document.getElementById('gmName');
  const newName = () => nameEl.textContent = pick(PRE) + ' ' + pick(STEM);
  document.getElementById('gmReroll').addEventListener('click', newName);

  /* =========================================================
     PRESETS / RANDOM / MAX
     ========================================================= */
  function loadPreset(k){
    const p = PRESETS[k]; S = {...p}; delete S.real;
    activePreset = k;
    [...presetEl.children].forEach(c => c.classList.toggle('on', c.textContent === k));
    nameEl.textContent = k;
    document.getElementById('gmDirty').textContent = '';
    render();
  }
  function dirty(){
    if (!activePreset) return;
    activePreset = null;
    [...presetEl.children].forEach(c => c.classList.remove('on'));
    document.getElementById('gmDirty').textContent = 'your own design';
    if (!/^(Republic|Free State|Grand Duchy|United Provinces|Kingdom|Federation|Commonwealth|Sovereign)/.test(nameEl.textContent)) newName();
  }
  function randomise(){
    const r = (a,b,dp=0) => +(a + Math.random()*(b-a)).toFixed(dp);
    S = {protein:r(30,125), dairy:r(0,380,0), gini:r(.22,.56,2), san:r(15,100), hc:r(10,100),
         ed:r(20,100), infect:r(0.5,10,1), air:r(6,110), meals:Math.random()<.5?1:0,
         uhc:Math.random()<.5?1:0, odf:Math.random()<.5?1:0, gen:1+Math.floor(Math.random()*3)};
    activePreset = null;
    [...presetEl.children].forEach(c => c.classList.remove('on'));
    document.getElementById('gmDirty').textContent = 'rolled at random';
    newName(); render();
  }
  function maxOut(){
    S = {protein:130, dairy:400, gini:.20, san:100, hc:100, ed:100, infect:0, air:5,
         meals:1, uhc:1, odf:1, gen:3};
    activePreset = null;
    [...presetEl.children].forEach(c => c.classList.remove('on'));
    document.getElementById('gmDirty').textContent = 'utopia mode';
    nameEl.textContent = 'Grand Duchy of Longshanks';
    render();
  }

  /* =========================================================
     RANKING STRIP (rebuilt when the reported sex changes)
     ========================================================= */
  let R_LO = 158, R_HI = 187;
  const rankEl = document.getElementById('gmRank');
  function buildRank(){
    R_LO = GSX === 'f' ? 146 : 158;
    R_HI = GSX === 'f' ? 175 : 187;
    let h = '<div class="rs-ax"></div>';
    REAL.forEach((r, i) => {
      const p = (r.v - R_LO)/(R_HI - R_LO)*100;
      h += `<div class="rs-t" style="left:${p.toFixed(1)}%"></div>`;
      if (i % 2 === 0 || r.c === 'NL') h += `<div class="rs-n" style="left:${p.toFixed(1)}%">${r.c}</div>`;
    });
    h += '<div class="rs-you" id="rsYou" data-l="YOU" style="left:0"></div>';
    rankEl.innerHTML = h;
  }
  buildRank();

  /* =========================================================
     RENDER
     ========================================================= */
  const figEl = document.getElementById('gmFig');
  figEl.innerHTML = `<line x1="2" y1="134" x2="58" y2="134" stroke="rgba(25,23,19,.5)" stroke-width="1.2"/>
    <svg id="gmBody" x="0" y="0" width="0" height="0" viewBox="0 0 30 162" preserveAspectRatio="none">
      <path d="${BODY}" fill="var(--red)"/></svg>`;

  let shown = null;
  function render(){
    // sync controls
    FIELDS.forEach(f => {
      const inp = document.getElementById('i-' + f.id);
      inp.value = S[f.id];
      const p = (S[f.id] - f.min)/(f.max - f.min)*100;
      document.getElementById('f-' + f.id).style.width = p.toFixed(1) + '%';
      const dec = f.dec || 0;
      document.getElementById('v-' + f.id).textContent = S[f.id].toFixed(dec) + f.u;
    });
    SWITCHES.forEach(s => {
      const b = document.getElementById('sw-' + s.id);
      b.classList.toggle('on', !!S[s.id]);
      b.setAttribute('aria-pressed', S[s.id] ? 'true' : 'false');
    });
    [...document.getElementById('gmGen').children].forEach(b =>
      b.classList.toggle('on', +b.dataset.g === S.gen));

    const M = model(S);
    const hM = M.h;                                // male-basis output of the machine
    const h = sexAdj(hM);                          // what the readout reports

    // number (short count animation); dataset carries the settled value
    const numEl = document.getElementById('gmNum');
    numEl.dataset.h = h.toFixed(1);
    const from = shown === null ? h : shown; shown = h;
    const t0 = performance.now();
    (function step(now){
      const p = Math.min((now - t0)/280, 1), e = 1 - Math.pow(1-p, 3);
      numEl.innerHTML = (from + (h - from)*e).toFixed(1) + '<small>CM</small>';
      if (p < 1) requestAnimationFrame(step);
    })(performance.now());

    // silhouette (scaled against the floor for the reported sex)
    const hp = ((h - (GSX === 'f' ? 138 : 150))/40) * 118 + 14;
    const body = document.getElementById('gmBody'), wpx = hp*(30/162);
    body.setAttribute('height', hp.toFixed(1));
    body.setAttribute('width', wpx.toFixed(1));
    body.setAttribute('x', (30 - wpx/2).toFixed(1));
    body.setAttribute('y', (134 - hp).toFixed(1));

    // rank placement
    const taller = REAL.filter(r => r.v > h).length;
    const rank = taller + 1;
    const above = REAL.filter(r => r.v > h).sort((a,b) => a.v - b.v)[0];
    const below = REAL.filter(r => r.v <= h).sort((a,b) => b.v - a.v)[0];
    document.getElementById('gmSub').innerHTML =
      `Would rank <b>#${rank}</b> of ${REAL.length + 1} · ` +
      (above && below ? `between ${below.c} ${below.v} and ${above.c} ${above.v}`
       : above ? `just under ${above.c} ${above.v}`
       : `taller than every nation on record`) +
      `<br>${(sexAdj(NL_MODEL) - h >= 0 ? (sexAdj(NL_MODEL) - h).toFixed(1) + ' cm below' : Math.abs(sexAdj(NL_MODEL) - h).toFixed(1) + ' cm above')}` +
      ` the same machine's Netherlands (${sexAdj(NL_MODEL).toFixed(1)})` +
      ` · reported for <b>${GSX === 'f' ? 'women' : 'men'}</b>`;
    document.getElementById('rsYou').style.left =
      Math.max(0, Math.min(100, (h - R_LO)/(R_HI - R_LO)*100)).toFixed(1) + '%';
    document.getElementById('gmRecord').classList.toggle('show', hM > NL_MODEL + 0.05);

    // waterfall
    const rows = Object.keys(M.cm).map(k => ({k, v: M.cm[k]})).sort((a,b) => b.v - a.v);
    const maxV = Math.max(...rows.map(r => r.v), 0.001);
    document.getElementById('gmWaterfall').innerHTML =
      `<div class="wf-row"><div class="wf-lb">Biological floor</div>
        <div class="wf-tr"><div class="wf-bar base" style="width:100%"></div></div>
        <div class="wf-vl">${sexAdj(BASE).toFixed(1)}</div></div>` +
      rows.map(r => `<div class="wf-row">
        <div class="wf-lb">${LABEL[r.k]}</div>
        <div class="wf-tr"><div class="wf-bar" style="width:${(r.v/maxV*100).toFixed(1)}%"></div></div>
        <div class="wf-vl ${r.v < 0.05 ? 'zero' : ''}">${r.v < 0.05 ? '—' : '+' + r.v.toFixed(1)}</div>
      </div>`).join('');

    // absorption
    const ab = Math.round(M.absorb*100);
    document.getElementById('gmAbs').textContent = ab + '%';
    document.getElementById('gmAbsBar').style.width = ab + '%';
    document.getElementById('gmAbsD').textContent = ab > 92
      ? 'Clean water and low infection: almost all the protein you buy turns into height.'
      : ab > 78 ? 'Some of the protein is being spent fighting infection instead of growing.'
      : 'Most of the food is being lost to infection. Fix the plumbing before you buy more milk.';

    // biggest lever left
    const room = [];
    FIELDS.forEach(f => {
      const best = {...S};
      best[f.id] = f.inv ? f.min : f.max;
      room.push({lb: f.lb, d: model(best).h - h});
    });
    SWITCHES.forEach(s => { if (!S[s.id]){ const b = {...S}; b[s.id] = 1; room.push({lb: s.lb, d: model(b).h - h}); } });
    if (S.gen < 3){ const b = {...S, gen:3}; room.push({lb:'Just keep going for three generations', d: model(b).h - h}); }
    room.sort((a,b) => b.d - a.d);
    document.getElementById('gmGap').textContent = '+' + room[0].d.toFixed(1) + ' cm';
    document.getElementById('gmGapD').textContent = room[0].lb + ' is where the most height is still sitting unused.';

    // reality check
    const rEl = document.getElementById('gmReality');
    const P = activePreset ? PRESETS[activePreset] : null;
    const realV = P ? (GSX === 'f' ? P.realF : P.real) : null;
    if (realV){
      const err = h - realV;
      rEl.innerHTML = `<em>Reality check</em>The machine says <b>${h.toFixed(1)} cm</b> for ${activePreset} ` +
        `(${GSX === 'f' ? 'women' : 'men'}). ` +
        `The tape measure says <b>${realV} cm</b> — the model is off by <b>${err >= 0 ? '+' : ''}${err.toFixed(1)} cm</b>. ` +
        `That miss is the honest part: eleven numbers cannot hold a country.`;
    } else {
      rEl.innerHTML = `<em>Reality check</em>No such country exists, so there is nothing to check it against. ` +
        `Load a preset to see how far the machine misses on a real nation — it is usually out by about <b>2 cm</b>, and sometimes by three.`;
    }
  }

  /* ---------- sex toggle ---------- */
  document.querySelectorAll('#gmSexM,#gmSexF').forEach(b => {
    b.addEventListener('click', () => {
      GSX = b.dataset.gsx;
      ['gmSexM','gmSexF'].forEach(id => {
        const el = document.getElementById(id), on = el.dataset.gsx === GSX;
        el.classList.toggle('on', on);
        el.setAttribute('aria-pressed', on ? 'true' : 'false');
      });
      syncReal();
      buildRank();
      shown = null;                                // don't animate across the sex jump
      render();
    });
  });

  NL_MODEL = model({...PRESETS['Netherlands, today']}).h;
  render();
})();
</script>

<!-- =================================================================
     PAGE 06 — MEASURE YOURSELF  (+ closing page controls)
     ================================================================= -->
<script>
(function(){
  /* closing-page control */
  const t = document.getElementById('toTop');
  if (t) t.addEventListener('click', () => window.scrollTo({top:0, behavior:'smooth'}));

  /* contents: mark whichever chapter is currently on screen */
  const links = [...document.querySelectorAll('.toc-l a')];
  const targets = links
    .map(a => ({a, el: document.querySelector(a.getAttribute('href'))}))
    .filter(o => o.el);
  if (!targets.length || !('IntersectionObserver' in window)) return;

  const seen = new Map();
  const mark = () => {
    let best = null;
    for (const o of targets){
      const r = seen.get(o.el) || 0;
      if (r > 0 && (!best || r > seen.get(best.el))) best = o;
    }
    links.forEach(a => a.removeAttribute('aria-current'));
    if (best) best.a.setAttribute('aria-current', 'true');
  };
  const io = new IntersectionObserver(es => {
    es.forEach(en => seen.set(en.target, en.intersectionRatio));
    mark();
  }, {threshold:[0, .12, .35, .6]});
  targets.forEach(o => io.observe(o.el));
})();
</script>
<!-- =================================================================
     Men / women controls: one visible segmented control per section,
     driving the existing per-section handler so the logic stays single-source.
     ================================================================= -->
<script>
(function(){
  document.querySelectorAll('.sexbar').forEach(bar => {
    const sec = bar.closest('section');
    const proxy = sec && sec.querySelector('.btn[data-proxy]');
    if (!proxy) return;
    const btns = [...bar.querySelectorAll('.sexbtn')];
    const isWomen = () => /Women/i.test(proxy.textContent);
    const sync = () => {
      const w = isWomen();
      btns.forEach(b => b.classList.toggle('on', (b.dataset.sx === 'w') === w));
      // a section can still declare itself male-only; none currently do
      const off = proxy.disabled;
      btns.forEach(b => { b.disabled = off; });
      bar.querySelector('.sexbar-n').style.opacity = off ? .55 : 1;
    };
    btns.forEach(b => b.addEventListener('click', () => {
      if (proxy.disabled) return;
      if ((b.dataset.sx === 'w') !== isWomen()) proxy.click();
      sync();
    }));
    // the section's own tabs can change availability, so re-sync on any click inside it
    // a section's own tabs can change availability; sync in the same frame, then again after
    sec.addEventListener('click', () => { sync(); setTimeout(sync, 0); });
    sync();
  });
})();
</script>
<script>
(function(){
  /* ==========================================================
     INCLUSIVITY LAYER
     · read aloud (for people who cannot read)
     · the same words on screen as a transcript (cannot hear)
     · a real data table per chapter (cannot see, or colour-blind)
     · text size, contrast, dyslexia-friendly font, stop motion
     ========================================================== */
  const CH = [{"key": "cover", "title": "What this is about", "say": "This page is about how tall people are. In some countries, people grow much taller than in others. It is not because of their families. It is because of food, clean water, doctors, and fair sharing. We looked at 196 countries. Our model uses only 11 development indicators and explains 96 percent of height differences.", "rows": ["Fact,Number", "Countries studied,196", "Birth cohorts in the model,31 (1970 to 2000)", "Development indicators,11", "How accurate the model is,0.96 out of 1", "Average error of the model,0.64 centimetres"]}, {"key": "frame", "title": "The bars: who grew, and by how much", "say": "Each bar is one country. A longer bar means taller people. Press play and the years move from 1900 to 1996. Only the last four points of each bar are measured numbers. The earlier ones are a reconstruction, because our height data starts in 1966. South Korea grew the most in this group, by about 15 centimetres. India grew the least, by about 4 centimetres. The United States started third and slipped to seventh place.", "rows": ["Country,Height in 1900 (reconstructed),Height in 1996 (measured),Change", "Netherlands,169.4 cm,183.5 cm,plus 14.1 cm", "Denmark,170.0 cm,181.3 cm,plus 11.3 cm", "Sweden,171.5 cm,180.2 cm,plus 8.7 cm", "Germany,169.0 cm,180.0 cm,plus 11.0 cm", "France,166.5 cm,178.2 cm,plus 11.7 cm", "United Kingdom,168.0 cm,177.9 cm,plus 9.9 cm", "United States,170.0 cm,176.5 cm,plus 6.5 cm", "Brazil,165.0 cm,175.0 cm,plus 10.0 cm", "South Korea,159.8 cm,174.6 cm,plus 14.8 cm", "China,161.5 cm,174.2 cm,plus 12.7 cm", "North Korea,159.5 cm,173.7 cm,plus 14.2 cm", "Japan,157.9 cm,171.9 cm,plus 14.0 cm", "Nigeria,160.0 cm,170.3 cm,plus 10.3 cm", "India,161.2 cm,165.4 cm,plus 4.2 cm", "Guatemala,155.0 cm,163.3 cm,plus 8.3 cm"]}, {"key": "map", "title": "The world map", "say": "This is a map of the whole world. Only the fifteen countries we follow closely are coloured in. A darker colour means taller people. All the other countries are flat grey: we still have their numbers, and you can still click them, but they are there for background. Every country on the map shows the same group: people born in 1996, measured at age 19. The tallest of the fifteen is the Netherlands. The shortest is Guatemala. You can switch between boys and girls.", "rows": ["Country,Height of 19 year old boys born in 1996", "Netherlands,183.5 cm", "Denmark,181.3 cm", "Sweden,180.2 cm", "Germany,180.0 cm", "France,178.2 cm", "United Kingdom,177.9 cm", "United States,176.5 cm", "Brazil,175.0 cm", "South Korea,174.6 cm", "China,174.2 cm", "North Korea,173.7 cm", "Japan,171.9 cm", "Nigeria,170.3 cm", "India,165.4 cm", "Guatemala,163.3 cm"]}, {"key": "mirrors", "title": "Two countries that were once one", "say": "North Korea and South Korea used to be one country. They split in 1945. The people are the same people. Men in the South are now about ten centimetres taller. These North Korean numbers come from measuring people who left North Korea, because almost nobody inside the country has been measured. People born before the split were actually a little taller in the North. Everyone born after it was shorter. India, China and Japan tell a second story. China is now the tallest of the three, even though Japan has about nine times more money per person.", "rows": ["Year,North Korea,South Korea,Gap", "1900,159.5 cm,159.8 cm,0.3 cm", "1940,163.5 cm,163.8 cm,0.3 cm", "1960,165.8 cm,167.2 cm,1.4 cm", "1970,165.2 cm,170.5 cm,5.3 cm", "1980,165.0 cm,173.5 cm,8.5 cm", "1996,165.6 cm,175.5 cm,9.9 cm"]}, {"key": "simulator", "title": "Build a pretend country", "say": "Here you can build a country that does not exist. Move the sliders to give it more doctors, more protein, cleaner water, and fairer sharing. The machine then guesses how tall the people would grow. The top three levers are: physician density, protein supply, and breastfeeding rate. This is a learning toy, not a real prediction.", "rows": ["Lever,What it changes,Importance", "Physician density,Access to healthcare,37 percent", "Protein in food,Building material for growth,13 percent", "Breastfeeding,Early nutrition sets the trajectory,10 percent", "Healthcare spending,System investment,7.5 percent", "Fair sharing of money,Helps the poorest children most,6.5 percent", "Clean air,Pollution stunts growth,5 percent"]}, {"key": "findings", "title": "What we learned", "say": "Height is the most honest progress report a nation can produce. Our model proved that 11 childhood development indicators explain 96 percent of why some nations are taller than others. Physician density is the number one driver at 37 percent. GDP per capita ranks only seventh. Being wealthy does not make a nation tall. Investing that wealth in healthcare and food does.", "rows": ["Finding,Detail", "Physician density,Ranked 1st at 37 percent importance", "Protein supply,Ranked 2nd at 13 percent", "Breastfeeding rate,Ranked 3rd at 10 percent", "GDP per capita,Ranked only 7th at 4.5 percent", "What genes explain between countries,Almost nothing — R squared 0.96 without any genetic data"]}];
  const MAP = [["section.hero", "cover"], ["#page02", "frame"], ["#page03", "map"], ["#page04", "mirrors"], ["#page05", "simulator"], ["#page06", "findings"]];
  const html = document.documentElement;

  /* ---------- skip link + landmark ---------- */
  const skip = document.createElement('a');
  skip.className = 'skip'; skip.href = '#a11y-start';
  skip.textContent = 'Skip to the story';
  document.body.insertBefore(skip, document.body.firstChild);
  const main = document.querySelector('main') || document.body;
  main.id = main.id || 'a11y-start';
  if (!main.hasAttribute('role')) main.setAttribute('role', 'main');

  /* ---------- a live region for anything that animates ---------- */
